  "answer_text": "## Spiegel Home Catalog & Online Shopping \u2014 What You Need to Know\n\n### \ud83d\udccb A Brief History of Spiegel\n\nSpiegel was an American direct marketing retailer founded in 1865 by Joseph Spiegel. The company published a catalog \u2014 like its competitors Sears, Aldens, and Montgomery Ward \u2014 advertising various brands of apparel, accessories, footwear, housewares, toys, tools, and electronics.\n\nSpiegel delivered its first mail-order catalog in 1905, and by 1925, the retailer had 10 million customers.\n\n---\n\n### \u274c Is Spiegel Still Operating?\n\nUnfortunately, **Spiegel is no longer in business.** Spiegel ran from 1865 to roughly 2019, when the brand quietly went dark under Patriarch Partners.\n\nAccording to archived references, the company abruptly ceased operations during the winter of 2019 to 2020. The website came down with no farewell letter, no closeout sale, and no press release of any consequence.\n\nAs of early 2026, spiegel.com does not resolve to a working storefront, there is no Spiegel print catalog being mailed in the United States, and no credible news of a brand revival, a buyer, or a relaunch could be found.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udecd\ufe0f Where to Find Spiegel Items Today\n\nEven though Spiegel itself is closed, you can still find Spiegel-related items through these channels:\n\n1. **eBay** \u2014 Great deals on Spiegel catalog items are available on eBay, with a large online selection and fast & free shipping on many items. Vintage catalogs from the 1950s\u20132000s are listed there.\n\n2. **Etsy** \u2014 Vintage Spiegel catalogs, such as a *1970 Fall/Winter Fashion Vintage Catalog* and rare 1972 Spiegel items, can be found on Etsy.\n\n3. **Vintage/Resale Sites** \u2014 Vintage Spiegel clothing turns up regularly on resale sites, and there is a small collector market for the older catalogs themselves on eBay.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udd04 Alternatives to Spiegel\n\nIf you're looking for a **similar shopping experience** to Spiegel, here are some still-active catalog retailers:\n\n**Talbots, Soft Surroundings, Appleseed's, and Roaman's** are all still operating and still mailing print catalogs in 2026.\n\nThese brands offer women's fashion and home goods in a style similar to what Spiegel once provided.\n\n---\n\n> \ud83d\udca1 **Tip:** If you held an unused Spiegel gift card or store credit, sadly that money is gone \u2014 Oak Point Partners acquired the remnant assets of the Signature Styles estate in 2012, and there is no consumer recourse at this point.",
